A global-cut benchmark instance is a finite undirected graph \(G=(V,E)\ningroup\) with nonnegative edge capacities \(c:E\to\mathbb R_{
obreak\ge0}\). For every nonempty proper subset \(S\subset V\), let \(\delta(S)=\{uv\in E:u\in S,
obreak v\notin S\}\) and \(c(\delta(S))=
obreak\sum_{e\in\delta(S)}c(e)\). The required value is \[\lambda(G)=\min_{
obreak\varnothing\ne S\subsetneq V}c(\delta(S)).\] A valid output is \((S,
obreak\lambda(G))\) attaining this minimum. No terminals, balance constraint, or locality restriction is imposed; disconnected graphs have value zero.
